    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "La 317ème Section stands as one of the most brutally realistic war films ever made, predating and influencing later Vietnam classics like <a href=\"/movie/792\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"792\">Platoon</a> (1986) and <a href=\"/movie/28\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"28\">Apocalypse Now</a> (1979). Director Pierre Schoendoerffer drew from his own experience as a military cameraman in Indochina to craft this stark portrayal of a doomed French patrol retreating through hostile territory during the final days of the First Indochina War. The film's documentary-like approach and unflinching depiction of jungle warfare created a template that later Vietnam War films would follow."
      },
      {
